  "report_period": "Week 39 (18th Sep to 25th Sep 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Chinese owners have committed the Capesize \"Highland\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS 03/2031, DD 01/2029) to Chinese interests at USD 25 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the two-years-older sister vessel \"NBA Peace\" 174/2004 SWS, China (SS/DD 04/2027) was sold at USD 19 mill. Silk Searoad Maritime have committed their Panamax \"Geneva Star\" 75/2009 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 01/2029, DD 04/2027) to Greek interests at USD 17 mill. Remind you that back in July, the one-year-older \"G. B. Corrado\" 77/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 03/2028) was sold at USD 15 mill. On the Supramax sector, Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha have committed their \"Ipsea Colossus\" 58/2011 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 01/2031, DD 01/2029) to undisclosed interests at USD 21 mill. Note that same owners sold the sister vessel \"Stenia Colossus\" 58/2011 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 03/2031, DD 04/2029) earlier this month at the same price. Campbell Shipping have committed the Handysize \"CS Calla\" 37/2011 Tianjin, China (SS/DD 10/2026, Ice Class 1C) at low-mid USD 11 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"Suzanna D\" 37/2012 Zhejiang, China (SS/DD 06/2027, Ice Class 1C) was sold in late June at USD 12,8 mill. Moreover, the \"IVS Kestrel\" 32/2014 Kanda, Japan (SS 05/2029, DD 05/2027, OHBS) was committed at USD 17 mill. By way of comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Crimson Wyoming\" 33/2015 Kanda, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 04/2028, OHBS) was committed a week ago at low USD 18 mill.",
    "tankers": "The VLCC \"Atherina\" 319/2011 Hyundai, Korea (SS 01/2031, DD 04/2029) was committed to clients of Sinokor at USD 146 mill, while the two-years- younger \"Seaking\" 319/2013 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 03/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed to clients of ADNOC at USD 177 mill. Ibaizabal Tankers have committed their Suezmax \"Montestena\" 159/2012 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 03/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 86 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Seaways Sabine\" 158/2012 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 07/2027) was committed a couple of weeks ago at USD 78 mill basis prompt delivery. The MR2 \"Ardmore Endeavour\" 49/2013 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 07/2028, Scrubber fitted) of Ardmore Shipping was committed to Turkish interests at USD 35 mill. Remind you that a couple of weeks ago, the one-year-younger \"LVM Aaron\" 50/2014 Dae Sun, Korea (SS 05/2029, DD 05/2027) was sold at USD 35,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route softened slightly, with Dampier to Qingdao fixtures settling between USD 16.25/16.75 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, achieved USD 43.50 fio. Transatlantic and regional Atlantic activity saw runs from Seven Islands to Praia Mole and Djen-Djen fixing between USD 26.50/27.25 fio, while a Narvik departure to Erdemir reached USD 23.75 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with South China and Singapore-Japan options settled between USD 19,500/20,000 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan, India and South East Asia ranges fetched between USD 19,000/26,000 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China, Japan and India achieved between USD 13,000/25,500 pd. From East Coast India and West Coast India, trips via South Africa to India obtained between USD 23,000/25,250 pd, while trips via ECSA to Singapore-Japan and South East Asia range fixed between USD 18,250/22,500 pd. A direct ECSA front-haul to Singapore-Japan reached USD 23,000 pd alongside a USD 1,300,000 ballast bonus. In the Atlantic, a West Med departure via USG to China reached USD 27,500 pd, alongside NCSA runs to Continent, Mediterranean and West Africa agreed between USD 21,300/22,400 pd. On period, a fixture for 7 to 9 months duration was secured at USD 23,500 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, Indonesian coal runs to South East Asia and ECI ranges settled between USD 20,000/23,000 pd and USD 28,000/29,000 pd respectively. An Australian grain run back to South East Asia fetched USD 24,500 pd, a North China trip via NoPac to ECI reached USD 26,000 pd, and a South China trip via PG to Mediterranean obtained USD 26,000 pd. Out of South East Asia, a cement run to West Africa fixed at USD 17,500 pd, while an ECI departure via Indonesia to India made USD 22,000 pd. In the Atlantic, a Continent run via Murmansk to US Gulf achieved USD 29,000 pd, alongside a long-haul petcoke trip from USEC to China reaching USD 34,500 pd. On period, a long- term fixture for 20 to 21 months duration was secured at USD 18,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Atlantic, ECSA grain runs to WCSA range secured strong levels between USD 29,500/31,500 pd, alongside a long-haul petcoke trip from ECSA to China fixing at USD 21,500 pd. Out of US Gulf, transatlantic grain departures to Mediterranean and Spain achieved between USD 25,000/28,000 pd, while a Caribs trip via US Gulf to EC Mexico made USD 14,000 pd. From USEC, a grain run via St Lawrence to NCSA range reached USD 21,000 pd."
    }
  },
